            <ArticleTitle>Analysis of the heavy-chain modification and TSG-6 activity in pathological hyaluronan matrices.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>543-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/978-1-4939-1714-3_42</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>During inflammation and developmental processes, heavy chains (HCs) from inter-α-inhibitor (IαI) are covalently transferred to hyaluronan (HA) via the enzyme tumor-necrosis-factor-stimulated-gene 6 (TSG-6) to form a HC-HA complex. In this manuscript, we describe a gel-based assay to detect HC-HA and TSG-6 activity in tissues.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
